#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369203 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064379 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2dbfe46-55f0-5d6a-b410-164f0aa2345f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Related Rate With a Circle: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94f771e8-4826-5b5d-8228-a990eba66454" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\text{ cm}\\text{/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369205} {:answer/id #uuid "75a1d081-eea5-5784-82dd-15b7ad720ca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5\\text{ cm}\\text{/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369206} {:answer/id #uuid "4f9a3ece-f0fc-5902-8ec9-1de1e79a9224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\text{ cm}\\text{/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369207} {:answer/id #uuid "fd7b5843-d568-544c-8d66-0fe759b8fdc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\text{ cm}\\text{/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369208} {:answer/id #uuid "73d4ba9d-d85b-5d24-b9bf-734a0c435e2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\text{ cm}\\text{/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75a1d081-eea5-5784-82dd-15b7ad720ca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5\\text{ cm}\\text{/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369206} :answer-field/id #uuid "2882600e-dd6b-59ca-8e2e-a290902aa712" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369204}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d90b811-f213-55fb-a391-b4b1340be2c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-116647" :question/problem "![](images/9a/9a864a350b6493794639ea031c7d40242717f5e7325eb326228f82a9cb1c10c9.png)\n\nA graphic designer is animating a circle in such a way that the area of the circle increases at a rate of $7\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}\\text{/s}.$ How fast is the radius of the circle increasing at the moment when the radius is $1\\text{ cm}?$" :question/worked-solution "In this situation, we want to find $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}$ at the moment when $r=1,$ and we are also told that  $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=7\\pi .$\n\nTo start, let's write down the area formula for the circle and then differentiate it using implicit differentiation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}r}(\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2\\pi r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=7\\pi $ and $r=1,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7\\pi  & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2\\pi (1) \\\\ 7\\pi  & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =3.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the radius is increasing at a rate of $3.5$ centimeters per second."}]}
